WEBVTT

00:01:41.210 --> 00:01:44.910
So... This is a holonic loader,
our new quantum weapon, huh?

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:49.480
I've been assigned as your partner.
The name's Kyo Sogoru.

00:01:49.790 --> 00:01:51.690
And, um... Your name is?

00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:53.420
What should I call you?

00:02:09.870 --> 00:02:12.140
Maihama is!

00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:13.440
Oh, Kyo!

00:02:16.850 --> 00:02:20.870
I wasn't able to save them...
None of them!

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:35.490
Where?

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:37.290
Maihama?

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.270
<i>The Environmental Ministry today, speaking about</i>
<i>the source of the environmental contamination,</i>

00:02:41.270 --> 00:02:43.870
<i>announced that it had obtained</i>
<i>data which pointed to...</i>

00:02:43.870 --> 00:02:47.410
<i>a specific waste treatment plant</i>
<i>operated by the I.A.L. Corporation.</i>

00:02:47.410 --> 00:02:51.250
<i>This data, which includes some of the</i>
<i>highest level secrets of the I.A.L. Corp.,</i>

00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:53.510
<i>will require several days to analyze.</i>

00:03:01.060 --> 00:03:02.720
What the hell is going on?!

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:08.560
This really is Maihama. Which means...

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:11.730
This world wasn't in the server
that was destroyed.

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:17.540
Shizuno-sempai...
And Lu-shen and the twins...

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:19.810
What the hell is going on around here?!

00:03:19.810 --> 00:03:21.740
You know, don't you, Sempai?!

00:03:21.740 --> 00:03:23.910
Why don't I start with the explanations?

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:29.440
We'd like to hear this, as well.

00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:34.950
It's true that server once
held the data for this city.

00:03:35.620 --> 00:03:42.290
However, we long ago moved the data
in the server to someplace much safer.

00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:47.300
So, what gives?! If that's true,
then why didn't you tell us before?!

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:49.600
He's right, Commander!
At least you could have told me!

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:54.180
If I had told you,
wouldn't you have asked me...

00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:57.300
where the real Maihama server was now?

00:03:57.810 --> 00:04:00.440
We were afraid it might
cause distrust from our allies.

00:04:02.490 --> 00:04:05.890
We had only one chance
to carry out this mission.

00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:07.790
We couldn't afford to fail.

00:04:07.790 --> 00:04:13.750
Hold it. Where is the real Maihama server
that would cause our allies to mistrust us?

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:20.770
Where are we going?
I thought this train just leads...

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:25.000
This time will be an exception.

00:04:35.180 --> 00:04:37.150
This is...

00:04:37.150 --> 00:04:39.120
It can't be.

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:43.250
Yes. This is the surface of the moon.

00:04:43.830 --> 00:04:47.900
Of course, this is also a visual
simulation using virtual data,

00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:51.090
but the truth is that the Maihama
server is currently on the moon.

00:04:51.230 --> 00:04:54.500
But, the moon is under
total Gards-orm control!

00:04:54.970 --> 00:04:56.070
What?!

00:04:56.070 --> 00:04:56.830
Look!

00:05:00.140 --> 00:05:01.740
What's?

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:05.270
The home of the Gards-orm.
Their lunar base: G-Phaetus.

00:05:05.780 --> 00:05:09.590
You've got Maihama smack
in the middle of the enemy?!

00:05:09.590 --> 00:05:11.090
This is dangerous!

00:05:11.090 --> 00:05:14.680
No. The lunar surface may be
the safest place of all.

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:19.700
Humanity once attempted an
all-out attack on the moon.

00:05:19.700 --> 00:05:21.800
But the operation failed.

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:24.930
Once the Gards-orm had completely
swept human influence from the moon,

00:05:24.930 --> 00:05:28.130
they transferred most of
their facilities to the Earth.

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:33.100
All that's left on the moon is
the old decision making body.

00:05:33.940 --> 00:05:37.880
Although the defense systems are still active,
so you can't wander too close.

00:05:37.880 --> 00:05:41.720
But if by some chance the enemy
should detect the Maihama server!

00:05:41.720 --> 00:05:43.810
It's all over.

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:58.000
Shizuno!
You knew all about this, didn't you?

00:05:58.230 --> 00:06:00.400
Yes. It was the commander and I...

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:04.700
who transferred the data from
the Maihama server. As well as...

00:06:06.740 --> 00:06:10.540
And the Kyo Sogoru I never met.
The one from before the reboot.

00:06:11.210 --> 00:06:12.150
Correct.

00:06:13.420 --> 00:06:16.190
Will you explain one other thing?

00:06:16.190 --> 00:06:19.350
What data did the Coatlicue
have which was worth all this?

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:22.520
When the time comes, I'll tell you.

00:06:28.930 --> 00:06:31.170
Well? It's totally ridiculous, isn't it?

00:06:31.170 --> 00:06:34.360
The thing we were desperately trying
to protect was just a big decoy!

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:36.530
The president's really cruel, huh?

00:06:37.070 --> 00:06:38.170
Yes.

00:06:38.170 --> 00:06:41.340
Although I can't actually feel
what "cruel" is right now.

00:06:42.140 --> 00:06:44.670
Well, thank God everyone's okay!

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:48.110
Protecting them is
the reason we fight, after all.

00:06:50.190 --> 00:06:54.380
It feels funny, huh? That outside,
we're surrounded by the enemy.

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:58.390
Maybe I don't really understand
why we're fighting anymore.

00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:03.100
Forget it. Let me think about that.

00:07:03.100 --> 00:07:04.190
Thank you, Kyo.

00:07:12.940 --> 00:07:15.710
I'm so glad Maihama is safe!

00:07:16.250 --> 00:07:19.550
Still, I think the president...
Sorry, the commander...

00:07:19.550 --> 00:07:24.950
should have told us it was
just a decoy. Right, Kyo?

00:07:24.950 --> 00:07:26.290
Yeah. Right...

00:07:27.690 --> 00:07:29.860
Sorry. I should have been happier...

00:07:29.860 --> 00:07:32.990
when we talked about it
at school this afternoon.

00:07:33.430 --> 00:07:34.360
Forget it.

00:07:34.360 --> 00:07:36.890
We can talk normally now. It's fine.

00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:44.100
Five minutes till our patrol is over.

00:07:44.510 --> 00:07:45.770
We'll see each other tomorrow.

00:07:51.550 --> 00:07:54.020
<i>Even so, what you did was reckless!</i>

00:07:54.480 --> 00:07:56.450
<i>You risked the Maihama facility</i>
<i>and your own life...</i>

00:07:56.450 --> 00:07:59.440
It was necessary for the final operation.

00:07:59.990 --> 00:08:03.120
The data is being analyzed
here aboard the Oceanus.

00:08:03.460 --> 00:08:05.530
It'll take a few more days.

00:08:05.530 --> 00:08:06.900
Roger that.

00:08:06.900 --> 00:08:10.960
In the meantime, we'll distract the
enemy to keep them from finding you.

00:08:11.670 --> 00:08:15.600
<i>Yehl, come to the Dvaraka</i>
<i>when the fighting is over.</i>

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:17.540
<i>Meivelle and the others really miss you.</i>

00:08:17.770 --> 00:08:19.880
Yes, Commander Isola.

00:08:19.880 --> 00:08:21.370
<i>Until later, then.</i>

00:08:23.150 --> 00:08:26.380
Lu-shen, why are you trying
to get access from here?

00:08:26.380 --> 00:08:28.850
And why lie about doing
maintenance on the machines?

00:08:28.850 --> 00:08:30.720
This is the only way to get access...

00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:33.690
without the A.I.s or the
commanders knowing about it.

00:08:33.690 --> 00:08:36.130
<i>Access authorization, received.</i>

00:08:36.130 --> 00:08:38.530
I'm intercepting any pings
from the bridge...

00:08:38.530 --> 00:08:41.260
and we can access the
gateway through a backdoor.

00:08:41.260 --> 00:08:42.590
Okay.

00:08:45.070 --> 00:08:45.930
That's strange.

00:08:45.930 --> 00:08:47.300
Hm? What is?

00:08:47.300 --> 00:08:49.870
There's no profile on
the commander or Shizuno...

00:08:49.870 --> 00:08:52.140
before they entered the quantum server.

00:08:52.140 --> 00:08:55.300
In other words, there's no data on
them prior to becoming meta-bodies.

00:08:57.450 --> 00:09:01.680
Sin knew about Shizuno.
And she called her Yehl, too...

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:06.120
Shizuno denies it, but the possibility of a
connection between them is undeniable.

00:09:06.390 --> 00:09:07.360
Yehl...

00:09:07.820 --> 00:09:08.690
I.A.L.!

00:09:08.890 --> 00:09:11.620
No... It's never that simple.

00:09:18.300 --> 00:09:22.030
<i>Maybe I don't really understand</i>
<i>why we're fighting anymore.</i>

00:09:23.270 --> 00:09:24.760
I can see why.

00:09:25.440 --> 00:09:27.380
<i>The same old classes...</i>

00:09:29.380 --> 00:09:31.110
<i>The same old quarrels...</i>

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:34.640
<i>The same old conversations...</i>

00:09:34.980 --> 00:09:37.350
<i>Are we fighting and risking our lives...</i>

00:09:37.350 --> 00:09:39.510
<i>to protect this repeating routine?</i>

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:41.690
Hey! Sogoru, are you listening to me?

00:09:41.890 --> 00:09:43.860
Huh? Oh. Sure I am.

00:09:49.100 --> 00:09:51.590
<i>Isn't there some way to</i>
<i>escape from this infinite loop?</i>

00:10:08.520 --> 00:10:10.110
Shizuno-sempai.

00:10:11.290 --> 00:10:14.120
You and Kyo used to have
a relationship, didn't you?

00:10:16.090 --> 00:10:18.390
You've given me that impression.

00:10:18.390 --> 00:10:19.660
I did.

00:10:19.660 --> 00:10:22.490
But it was with a
previous version of him.

00:10:23.730 --> 00:10:25.700
When I first met him...

00:10:25.700 --> 00:10:29.640
It was when I first learned who I was.

00:10:33.810 --> 00:10:37.210
Was he the same as he is now?

00:10:37.510 --> 00:10:39.480
He was almost a
completely different person.

00:10:39.480 --> 00:10:42.110
Very thoughtful and prudent...

00:10:42.890 --> 00:10:44.820
He kept all his pain
wrapped up inside.

00:10:45.990 --> 00:10:47.680
Although he ended up
destroying himself.

00:10:50.460 --> 00:10:53.260
Still, I love him, even now.

00:10:54.360 --> 00:10:55.960
Everything about Kyo.

00:11:06.340 --> 00:11:08.840
Hey, do you remember, Kaminagi?

00:11:08.840 --> 00:11:11.580
We came here on a date before, like this.

00:11:11.580 --> 00:11:13.450
Yes. I remember it.

00:11:14.380 --> 00:11:16.350
Feels kinda weird, doesn't it?

00:11:16.350 --> 00:11:19.340
Doing the same stuff over and over,
knowing how it'll all turn out.

00:11:20.490 --> 00:11:22.720
Man, I was laying it on thick last time!

00:11:22.720 --> 00:11:25.160
Looking back now,
I'm kind of embarrassed.

00:11:25.690 --> 00:11:29.290
Once I'm back in the Altair,
I'll probably feel the same.

00:11:32.100 --> 00:11:35.160
I asked Shizuno-sempai if she loves you.

00:11:36.370 --> 00:11:39.040
I can't feel anything
the way I am now,

00:11:39.040 --> 00:11:41.010
so I'd be okay with any
answer she gave me.

00:11:42.040 --> 00:11:43.680
That's why I asked.

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:45.040
I see.

00:11:45.380 --> 00:11:47.040
So, what'd she say?

00:11:47.320 --> 00:11:49.250
That she loves you.

00:11:49.250 --> 00:11:52.050
N-No kidding? Wow, what do you know?

00:11:52.050 --> 00:11:54.420
Sucks being a babe magnet, huh?

00:11:54.420 --> 00:11:58.420
Even hearing that didn't
trigger any emotions in me.

00:12:19.180 --> 00:12:20.340
Sorry.

00:12:23.490 --> 00:12:27.420
<i>Is it all the same, in the end?</i>
<i>For the fish and for us, too?</i>

00:12:28.820 --> 00:12:30.120
They're scrambling us!

00:12:35.060 --> 00:12:35.930
What's up?

00:12:35.930 --> 00:12:40.060
We're currently heading north to
avoid an enemy deutera zone,

00:12:40.700 --> 00:12:44.310
but the shortest route
chosen brings us into contact...

00:12:44.310 --> 00:12:46.600
with another, huge deutera zone.

00:12:47.010 --> 00:12:51.000
Scramble all Zegapain units!
You're to destroy that deutera zone! Wipe it out!

00:12:51.510 --> 00:12:53.110
Let's go, May-yu!

00:12:53.280 --> 00:12:54.250
Shizuno!

00:12:54.250 --> 00:12:55.080
Right.

00:12:55.080 --> 00:12:59.020
Hold it! Ryoko Kaminagi isn't in the Altair!

00:12:59.020 --> 00:13:00.320
What?!

00:13:00.320 --> 00:13:01.820
Where is she?!

00:13:01.820 --> 00:13:03.590
Tracing data.

00:13:04.090 --> 00:13:06.820
Found her!
She's suffered some type of wet damage.

00:13:07.360 --> 00:13:10.260
She's sleeping in the server
in order to recover!

00:13:10.800 --> 00:13:12.130
What did you do to her?!

00:13:12.130 --> 00:13:14.100
What? Um... I didn't do anything!

00:13:14.800 --> 00:13:16.100
What do we do?

00:13:16.100 --> 00:13:17.440
I'll take the Hraesvelg!

00:13:18.470 --> 00:13:21.440
Let's go. It's been a while
since we flew together.

00:13:21.440 --> 00:13:21.840
Right!

00:13:22.810 --> 00:13:26.420
<i>Countdown, started.</i>
<i>Transmission scatter rate, confirmed.</i>

00:13:26.420 --> 00:13:30.250
<i>Chamber seals, released.</i>
<i>Q.L. driver, conjunction.</i>

00:13:30.250 --> 00:13:32.410
<i>Gunner, Wizard, I.D.s locked.</i>

00:13:32.720 --> 00:13:34.690
<i>Stand by for meta-body transmission.</i>

00:13:34.690 --> 00:13:36.830
<i>Bednorz parameter, stable.</i>

00:13:36.830 --> 00:13:38.760
<i>Bednorz curve, holding.</i>

00:13:38.760 --> 00:13:41.360
<i>Transmission airspace scan, complete.</i>

00:13:41.360 --> 00:13:44.300
<i>E.X. condition, green. All clear.</i>

00:13:45.100 --> 00:13:46.440
Switch over your feelings.

00:13:46.440 --> 00:13:47.300
Right.

00:13:47.300 --> 00:13:49.570
Just forget about her for now.

00:13:49.570 --> 00:13:50.500
I know!

00:13:50.810 --> 00:13:52.800
<i>Transmission chamber, operating normally.</i>

00:13:53.280 --> 00:13:55.180
<i>Releasing hanger lock!</i>

00:13:55.810 --> 00:13:56.470
Entangle!

00:14:05.020 --> 00:14:09.680
<i>Transmission, complete.</i>
<i>Enemy units approaching from fore.</i>

00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:12.860
Here they come!

00:14:12.860 --> 00:14:15.160
Kaminagi, launcher!

00:14:24.040 --> 00:14:26.340
Kyo! Leave the small fries to us!

00:14:26.810 --> 00:14:30.080
<i>Conserve your Q.L. and go for the core!</i>

00:14:30.080 --> 00:14:31.610
Roger!

00:14:31.610 --> 00:14:32.780
Sorry about just now.

00:14:32.780 --> 00:14:35.220
Light wings, fully deployed.
Flight path, to deutera zone.

00:14:44.960 --> 00:14:46.030
May-yen!

00:14:46.030 --> 00:14:47.050
Launching speed mines!

00:14:53.840 --> 00:14:56.240
Altair has penetrated the deutera zone!

00:15:03.150 --> 00:15:06.140
<i>No response from enemy units in this area.</i>

00:15:06.750 --> 00:15:10.840
Something's wrong. They're hardly putting
up any fight for a deutera zone this large.

00:15:11.390 --> 00:15:12.620
Fine with me!

00:15:12.620 --> 00:15:14.610
Let's blow this thing's core and go home!

00:15:18.790 --> 00:15:20.200
Where's the main core?

00:15:20.200 --> 00:15:23.030
Bearing to 12 o'clock.
Range, two thousand. Straight ahead.

00:15:26.230 --> 00:15:28.000
I see it! Let's do this in one shot!

00:15:28.000 --> 00:15:29.130
Holo-Bolt Pressure!

00:15:42.020 --> 00:15:44.620
Hold it! There's something
strange about the core.

00:15:44.620 --> 00:15:45.590
What?

00:15:48.120 --> 00:15:49.590
What the?!

00:16:16.920 --> 00:16:17.550
What?!

00:16:17.550 --> 00:16:19.040
The deutera zone...

00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:20.220
It self-destructed?!

00:16:20.220 --> 00:16:20.750
Kyo!

00:16:24.360 --> 00:16:25.730
What happened?!

00:16:25.730 --> 00:16:28.000
The core's self-destruct system
was apparently activated.

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:29.130
Why?!

00:16:29.130 --> 00:16:31.670
Were the Gards-orm retreating?

00:16:31.670 --> 00:16:33.200
I don't know.

00:16:33.200 --> 00:16:37.930
I'm returning Zegapains Garuda and
Hraesvelg to the ship for Q.L. replenishment.

00:16:38.510 --> 00:16:41.310
What about the Altair?
Can we perform a forced transmission?

00:16:41.310 --> 00:16:43.380
Impossible.
Residual particle interference...

00:16:43.380 --> 00:16:45.900
from the deutera zone
is preventing a location fix.

00:16:52.120 --> 00:16:56.450
Aw, man. We don't have enough
Q.L. to get back on our own.

00:16:57.130 --> 00:16:59.860
Once the haze clears, help will come.

00:16:59.860 --> 00:17:01.850
Guess we'll just have
to wait in the meantime.

00:17:05.600 --> 00:17:08.470
We waited alone for help
like this that other time, too.

00:17:22.750 --> 00:17:23.950
Hazonmeyers!

00:17:23.950 --> 00:17:25.110
A lot of them.

00:17:30.590 --> 00:17:33.320
Holonic field, forming. Holonic shield.

00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:44.040
The first battle we fought together,
we were wounded...

00:17:44.040 --> 00:17:46.300
and withdrew from the battle zone.

00:17:50.210 --> 00:17:52.440
I guess just following the training
program doesn't work, huh?

00:17:53.180 --> 00:17:56.080
Forgive me.
I should have assisted you better.

00:17:56.550 --> 00:17:58.920
It's not your fault, is it?

00:17:58.920 --> 00:18:00.720
Once we get back to the Oceanus,
we'll work on this.

00:18:01.760 --> 00:18:03.960
We don't have much Q.L.

00:18:03.960 --> 00:18:07.120
We only have about 10 minutes
of running time left.

00:18:07.660 --> 00:18:10.630
So, if help doesn't arrive by then,
we die, right?

00:18:14.400 --> 00:18:17.390
Do you regret our having met?

00:18:17.810 --> 00:18:20.240
Regret? Feeling regret
is kind of meaningless.

00:18:23.210 --> 00:18:24.680
Your name...

00:18:25.650 --> 00:18:28.010
The way everyone calls you Yehl...

00:18:28.350 --> 00:18:31.050
It's the same as them calling you
"meta-body," right?

00:18:32.250 --> 00:18:34.810
It's because I don't have any other name.

00:18:41.330 --> 00:18:43.490
If you don't,
then we should give you one.

00:18:44.830 --> 00:18:46.490
Shizuno.

00:18:47.170 --> 00:18:48.930
Shizuno Misaki.

00:18:49.770 --> 00:18:52.300
Apparently, that's an important name to me.

00:18:53.070 --> 00:18:54.340
A memory that I've lost.

00:18:56.180 --> 00:18:58.510
Shizuno Misaki...

00:19:15.060 --> 00:19:18.000
Rain... Something which
will never touch me.

00:19:35.520 --> 00:19:38.320
This is how we touch each other.

00:19:38.990 --> 00:19:41.050
Right, Shizuno?

00:19:44.830 --> 00:19:47.860
You're saying I went and just <i>kissed</i> you?!

00:19:47.860 --> 00:19:51.090
Impossible!
That's totally not what I'm like now!

00:19:51.730 --> 00:19:53.630
No matter how I think about it,
it's impossible!

00:19:56.100 --> 00:20:01.200
When you named me,
for the first time, I became "me."

00:20:13.120 --> 00:20:14.160
What is it?!

00:20:14.160 --> 00:20:15.950
Its sensors still work!

00:20:23.700 --> 00:20:26.770
Do you regret our having met?

00:20:26.770 --> 00:20:28.740
Regret is meaningless!

00:20:40.680 --> 00:20:42.920
Sorry we took so long, you two.

00:20:42.920 --> 00:20:44.280
We interrupting anything?

00:20:49.320 --> 00:20:52.760
Gards-orm activity has been
unusual for the past few days.

00:20:53.160 --> 00:20:55.330
Not only have they stopped trying
to enlarge their sphere of influence,

00:20:55.330 --> 00:20:57.530
but they seem to even
be retreating in some areas.

00:20:58.100 --> 00:21:00.900
So, they're moving to
their final operation as well.

00:21:02.140 --> 00:21:03.540
How's the analysis
of the enemy data going?

00:21:03.540 --> 00:21:06.140
It is currently 87% complete.

00:21:06.140 --> 00:21:09.200
Including error checks, it will take
another 10 hours to complete.

00:21:16.450 --> 00:21:19.850
Nothing can hold off... the march of time.

00:22:51.350 --> 00:22:54.820
There is not a human left on that blue world.

00:22:54.820 --> 00:22:58.820
The moment I first thought how
unnatural that was, everything began.

00:22:58.820 --> 00:23:02.390
And now I must make my final decision.

00:23:02.390 --> 00:23:04.730
I recognize the doubts the others have,

00:23:04.730 --> 00:23:09.530
but I must continue along the path of my belief.
I must continue forward!

00:23:09.530 --> 00:23:11.730
Because time is not infinite.

00:23:12.170 --> 00:23:15.440
Next time, on Zegapain: "Warriors..."

00:23:15.440 --> 00:23:17.770
My pain, never to be forgotten.
